    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/633804AB.JPG\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 145px;\" /><br />The shortest distance <math><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math> occurs along the common normal;<br />i.e., when <math><mi>P</mi></math> is <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced></math> &amp; <math><mi>Q</mi></math> is <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0,2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math><br />Hence <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>minimum</mi></msub></math><math><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math>",
